  every state s has an unconditional exit s -> (numerator) listed before the first no-state fraction (#12): True  exits: [(11, (13, 11)), (13, (11, 13)), (17, (1, 17)), (19, (77, 19)), (23, (95, 23)), (29, (77, 29))]
  fractions that add a state without removing one: [(55, 1)] (no-state fractions, so they act only when no state is present)
  => by induction from 2 (no state), the state part of every configuration is zero or one prime to the first power (PROVED by the two checks above).

