(3) CONWAY list (Conway 1987, Guy 1983): the machine table (a 4-register Minsky machine, states = state primes, 1 = no state)
====================================================================================================
  state 1:
      fraction #12 if r2>0 and r7>0          then r2-=1, r7-=1, r3+=1, r5+=1   -> state 1
      fraction #13 if r2>0                   then r2-=1, r3+=1, r5+=1          -> state 1
      fraction #14 if always                 then r5+=1                        -> state 11
  state 11:
      fraction #5  if r3>0                   then r3-=1                        -> state 29
      fraction #11 if always                 then no register change           -> state 13
  state 13:
      fraction #1  if r7>0                   then r7-=1                        -> state 17
      fraction #10 if always                 then no register change           -> state 11
  state 17:
      fraction #2  if r5>0                   then r5-=1, r2+=1, r3+=1          -> state 13
      fraction #3  if r3>0                   then r3-=1                        -> state 19
      fraction #9  if always                 then no register change           -> state 1
  state 19:
      fraction #4  if r2>0                   then r2-=1                        -> state 23
      fraction #8  if always                 then r7+=1                        -> state 11
  state 23:
      fraction #7  if always                 then r5+=1                        -> state 19
  state 29:
      fraction #6  if always                 then r7+=1                        -> state 11
